llows. Since propertyAP is preserved under extensions, Γ has property-AP, and we can argue as before to conclude the proof.\n\nRemark 5.5. Our proof will show that Γ = Γ1 × Γ2 × . . . × Γn has C∗-ISR property if every Γi is a torsion-free non-amenable acylindrically hyperbolic group with property-AP.\n\n",
