      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.11588398692810459,
        "y0": 0.8150707070707071,
        "x1": 0.8840245098039216,
        "y1": 0.8667979797979798
      },
      "text": "Since A is invariant, it follows that (g, h) = tn1 ⊗ tm2 ∈ A. The claim follows. Since propertyAP is preserved under extensions, Γ has property-AP, and we can argue as before to conclude the proof.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
